(Quick Hit:) Tj
T*
(The Menu plays like a razor-edged satire nightmare?sharp, funny, with enough style to make ) Tj
T*
(the damage look beautiful.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Full Take:) Tj
T*
(The Menu leans hard into satire horror energy, and Mark Mylod keeps the tone sharp without ) Tj
T*
(letting the movie drift. The filmmaking is locked in, the atmosphere is doing real work, and) Tj
T*
( the payoff earns the damage. It may not be for everybody, but it definitely has teeth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
